Workflow inspired by ScanTailor and ScanTailor Advanced (GPL-3.0) — thank you to their
developers; no code from them is used.

  ScanTailor:          https://github.com/scantailor/scantailor
  ScanTailor Advanced: https://github.com/4lex4/scantailor-advanced

The ink threshold follows N. Otsu, "A Threshold Selection Method from Gray-Level
Histograms", IEEE Transactions on Systems, Man, and Cybernetics, SMC-9(1):62-66, 1979.

Built on Pillow (MIT-CMU licence): https://python-pillow.org

Skew, page box and content box (spec 0004)

  The skew estimate scores projection profiles, after W. Postl, "Detection of linear
  oblique structures and skew scan in digitized documents", Proc. International
  Conference on Pattern Recognition, 1986, and H. S. Baird, "The skew angle of printed
  documents", Proc. SPSE Symposium on Hybrid Imaging Systems, 1987. Its cross-check by a
  second estimator follows finding 0009, which cites D. S. Le, G. R. Thoma and
  H. Wechsler, "Automated page orientation and skew angle detection for binary document
  images", Pattern Recognition, 1994.

  Bands, blobs and border shadows are removed by reconstruction from markers, after
  L. Vincent, "Morphological grayscale reconstruction in image analysis: applications
  and efficient algorithms", IEEE Transactions on Image Processing, 1993.

  The page box walks in from the frame's sides, after the page-frame detection of
  F. Shafait, J. van Beusekom, D. Keysers and T. M. Breuel, "Document cleanup using page
  frame detection", International Journal on Document Analysis and Recognition, 2008,
  and K.-C. Fan, Y.-K. Wang and T.-R. Lay, "Marginal noise removal of document images",
  Pattern Recognition, 2002.

  These detectors use Otsu's threshold, credited above.
